    <section>
      <h2>Total Revenue</h2>
      <p class="narrative">Headline revenue with its three fee engines. Component definitions vary by filer — trading revenue in particular splits across different XBRL concepts — so trend shape within a bank is more reliable than cross-bank levels.</p>
      <div class="chart-grid cols-2">
      <figure class="chart-block">
        <figcaption>
          <h3>Total Revenue</h3>
          <span class="unit">USD billions</span>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="canvas-wrap"><canvas data-metric="Total Revenue"></canvas></div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="chart-block">
        <figcaption>
          <h3>Net Interest Income</h3>
          <span class="unit">USD billions</span>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="canvas-wrap"><canvas data-metric="Net Interest Income"></canvas></div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="chart-block">
        <figcaption>
          <h3>Investment Banking Fees</h3>
          <span class="unit">USD billions</span>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="canvas-wrap"><canvas data-metric="Investment Banking Fees"></canvas></div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="chart-block">
        <figcaption>
          <h3>Trading Revenue</h3>
          <span class="unit">USD billions</span>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="canvas-wrap"><canvas data-metric="Trading Revenue"></canvas></div>
      </figure></div>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Net Income</h2>
      <p class="narrative">The bottom line and its per-share expression. Diluted EPS reflects buybacks as well as earnings, which is why the EPS trend can outrun net income.</p>
      <div class="chart-grid cols-2">
      <figure class="chart-block">
        <figcaption>
          <h3>Net Income</h3>
          <span class="unit">USD billions</span>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="canvas-wrap"><canvas data-metric="Net Income"></canvas></div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="chart-block">
        <figcaption>
          <h3>EPS (Diluted)</h3>
          <span class="unit">$ / share</span>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="canvas-wrap"><canvas data-metric="EPS (Diluted)"></canvas></div>
      </figure></div>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Consumer Credit Quality</h2>
      <p class="narrative">Three proxies read together: provisions (the forward-looking P&L charge), the allowance (the balance-sheet reserve), and net charge-offs (realized losses). Provisions rising ahead of charge-offs signals management expects deterioration; the reverse signals releases.</p>
      <div class="chart-grid cols-2">
      <figure class="chart-block">
        <figcaption>
          <h3>Provision for Credit Losses</h3>
          <span class="unit">USD billions</span>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="canvas-wrap"><canvas data-metric="Provision for Credit Losses"></canvas></div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="chart-block">
        <figcaption>
          <h3>Net Charge-Offs</h3>
          <span class="unit">USD billions</span>
        </figcaption>
        <div class="canvas-wrap"><canvas data-metric="Net Charge-Offs"></canvas></div>
      </figure></div>
    </section>

